  Method: every leg carries the subject group, a control group that was never joined and
  must NOT arrive, and an instrument control (routed ICMP unicast 10.38.22.40 ->
  10.38.22.65) that must always arrive. The instrument control arrived at FULL count in
  all 11 counted legs of this case, so every zero below is a measurement and not a dead
  capture. Every group address used is distinct in its low 23 bits, so no two share a
  link-layer address and no count can bleed between groups.
  A bench note for anyone repeating this (O-26): a capture on a switched VLAN of this
  DUT competes with a 1 Hz loop-detect LDF stream (`loop-protection loop-detect
  ldf-interval 1 fast-block` is in the baseline config). Those are 802.3/LLC
  `Null Unnumbered, test` frames with no IP header, and an unfiltered `tcpdump -c 24` is
  consumed by them in under half a minute. A bare `ip` qualifier excludes every one of
  them while keeping PIM, IGMP and the multicast data.

