STEP 1 -- PIM-DM brought up on the DUT and on sw1 (designed)                       PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: AW+ gates the routing daemons on a licensed `service`, sent alone. PIM-SM was
  fully removed before this case began, so the bench started multicast-OFF.

swi_d(config)#service pdm           accepted, 17:01 (no error)
swi_a(config)#service pdm           accepted, 17:01 (no error)
awplus#show process | include pdm
 3343 pdmd                5   0.0   0.1    20 sleep        <-- the daemon IS running

  The same command on swi_b is what rules it out as `sw1`:

x960-28YSQ(config)#service pdm
% Service is not currently licensed on this platform

  Router-side IGMP was included in this case's setup from the start, and it still bit --
  which confirms the mechanism rather than contradicting it. The baseline join at
  17:01:45 was sent BEFORE the `ip igmp` line was applied, so it landed in the snooping
  table only and the first forwarding leg read 0 of 10 for a group that looked joined
  (STEP 2, leg 3a). Re-joining AFTER `ip igmp` was enabled gave 10 of 10 with nothing
  else changed. A membership learned while the interface was snoop-only does NOT migrate
  when router-side IGMP is later enabled -- it must be re-sent.

swi_a#show ip igmp interface vlan48
