cap d8-graft-eth4.pcap: 41 frame(s)
  x20 UDP  10.38.22.40 -> 239.11.11.11 :5001 [ours] [eth 88:9d:98:df:26:02 -> 01:00:5e:0b:0b:0b]
  x20 ICMP t8/c0 10.38.22.40 -> 10.38.22.65 [ours] (20/20 instrument control)

  => STEP 5 PASS: 0 of 50 while pruned becomes 20 of 20 once grafted -- same group, same
     source, same wire, one IGMP report as the only variable -- and the handshake that
     did it is on the wire: a UNICAST Graft from `sw1` to the DUT, answered by a UNICAST
     Graft Acknowledgement 206 microseconds later, exactly as RFC 3973 section 4.6
     specifies. This is the limb that makes the case PIM-DM rather than "multicast".

